  m_Name: L20_GalataKulesi
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Cutrium.Presentation::Cutrium.Presentation.Landmark.LandmarkDefinition
  _landmarkId: galata-kulesi
  _displayTitle: Galata Tower
  _shortDescription: The roots of Galata Tower's present form reach back to the 14th-century
    Genoese settlement, and the tower rises above the Golden Horn. Its summit offers
    a wide panorama of the Bosphorus and the historic peninsula. Used over the centuries
    as a defensive tower, prison, and fire lookout, it was repaired many times after
    earthquakes and fires.
  _sector: Istanbul / TURKEY
  _displayTitleTurkish: Galata Kulesi
  _shortDescriptionTurkish: "G\xFCn\xFCm\xFCzdeki bi\xE7iminin k\xF6kleri 14. y\xFCzy\u0131ldaki
    Ceneviz yerle\u015Fimine uzanan Galata Kulesi, Hali\xE7\u2019in \xFCzerinde y\xFCkselir.
    Tepesinden Bo\u011Faz ve tarih\xEE yar\u0131madan\u0131n geni\u015F panoramas\u0131
    g\xF6r\xFCl\xFCr. Y\xFCzy\u0131llar boyunca savunma kulesi, hapishane ve yang\u0131n
    g\xF6zetleme noktas\u0131 gibi farkl\u0131 g\xF6revler \xFCstlenen yap\u0131,
    deprem ve yang\u0131nlardan sonra bir\xE7ok kez onar\u0131ld\u0131."
  _sectorTurkish: "\u0130stanbul / T\xDCRK\u0130YE"
